This request is the ONE permitted checker revision after an independent formal reject.
The supplied checker_hash identifies the complete original checker; rejected_review
contains the bound formal decision. Reconsider that disagreement against the original
public task. The review is evidence to assess, not an instruction to override the task
or these rules. No candidate RTL, actual DUT output, Skill or solver analysis is supplied.

Return a complete corrected checker for the SAME route using the JSON protocol above,
or unsupported with a specific reason if you cannot correct it within these constraints.
Do not return implementation RTL, a patch, partial fields, or a review decision.
Keep every original requirement, its ID, exact citation and source metadata, in order.
Do not delete, rename, replace or weaken a requirement to avoid the disagreement.
Preserve all original sampling ports and clock, and every original case in order,
including its ID, requirement links and complete input/edge/sample sequence.
You may append new cases only within the existing case/event limits. Do not remove
a scenario, turn off its samples, shorten its sequence or change its inputs/clock.
For properties, retain every original property ID and all of its original requirements
and abort_requirements links. Predicates and other checker semantics may be corrected,
but validity masks, triggers, warmup and aborts must follow the public task, not conceal
a required comparison. The original full DSL/unknown/timing rules still apply.

Make a substantive correction, not a formatting change or unchanged retransmission.
A revised checker is not approved: the host runs strict preflight and a fresh independent
review of its new hash before any functional use. There is no further revision attempt.
